--- a/benchmarks/README.md
+++ b/benchmarks/README.md
@@ -54,6 +54,23 @@ route roles, models, expected efforts, and observed efforts are required. The
 single-Sol control and Astral treatment may intentionally use different route settings;
 the scorecard compares their outcomes, not identical model configurations.
 
+Before a run, use the effort configurator's read-only check mode to verify the frozen
+lane settings. Pass one or more `--expect lane=value` arguments; `--check` always emits
+JSON, exits zero only when every expectation matches the effective settings, and never
+creates or changes the supplied settings file.
+
+```sh
+python3 plugins/astral-orchestrator/scripts/configure-effort.py \
+  --settings-file /path/to/effort-levels.toml \
+  --check \
+  --expect orchestrator=high \
+  --expect terra=xhigh
+```
+
+The JSON report includes the effective and expected values, a `matched` boolean, and a
+`mismatches` object. A missing settings file is checked against Astral's defaults and
+remains missing.
+
 The control is `single-sol`: one Sol route. The treatment is `astral`: an orchestrator,
 at least one Luna or Terra worker, and a fresh Sol reviewer. Record observed route facts
 for every lane rather than assuming that a task label proves its model or effort.
